[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Hold {start} to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {r3} to recenter it.
Flick stick: push the right stick {rs} toward where you want to face and the view turns to it; turn it around the rim to keep turning. The gyro aims up, down and finely.
{start} (Escape) pauses and backs out of the game's menus. The campaign has no quick save; it saves at checkpoints.
The buttons follow the Xbox 360 release's default layout. {south} jumps, {east} crouches and a long press of {east} goes prone, {west} reloads and, held, uses: pick up a weapon, plant, open doors. {north} switches weapons.
{lb} throws your tactical grenade (flash, stun, smoke) and {rb} your lethal one: hold to cook a frag, let go to throw. Hold {l3} to sprint, and while aiming hold it to steady a sniper rifle. {r3} is melee.
{up} switches night vision on and off, {left} the underbarrel attachment (grenade launcher, shotgun), {right} calls in a killstreak and {down} takes out your equipment. Hold {select} for the scoreboard and objectives.
Chat in multiplayer needs typing: open the on-screen keyboard with {guide} + {west} and press T (all) or Y (team).
Online play: the original servers are unsafe, so most players use the IW4x client. IW4x has controller support of its own; if you turn it on there, don't use this setup at the same time, or the two would fight. On the Steam servers, VAC sees the pad as an ordinary keyboard and mouse.
These are the game's default PC keys, written from memory and not checked in the game (melee, the grenades and the D-pad's attachment, killstreak and equipment keys especially). Compare them with Options → Controls and change the buttons here to match. The gyro's real-world turn assumes the default mouse sensitivity of 5; set the full turn to 16364 divided by your sensitivity.'''

